cuems-common (1.3.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * rtpmidid.service.d/cuems-node-group.conf: order rtpmidid after avahi-daemon
    (Wants=+After=avahi-daemon.service) so its libavahi-client connects to a
    ready daemon and publishes its _apple-midi services. On cold boot rtpmidid
    was starting ~170ms before avahi-daemon, deferring its registration and
    (pre rtpmidid 26.06~1stagelab1) never committing it -> controller invisible
    over mDNS, nodes never discover its MTC export, nodes get no MTC. Pairs with
    the rtpmidid announce_all()-on-S_RUNNING fix. Deliberately avoids
    network-online.target (documented ordering-cycle trap above the new lines).

