cuems-common (1.3.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sudoers: add 99-cuems-admin-poweroff granting cuems-admin passwordless
    /sbin/poweroff. cuems-power-bridge now SSHes nodes as cuems-admin (which
    has a login shell) instead of the nologin cuems service user; this lets
    the unattended, no-TTY poweroff complete. Scoped to poweroff only — full
    cuems-admin sudo still requires a password. New file (not an edit of
    99-cuems-poweroff) to avoid a conffile prompt on upgrade. The bridge key
    is additionally locked to this one command via a forced-command entry in
    cuems-admin's authorized_keys (shipped by cuems-power-bridge deploy-keys).

